{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CftBJt3HK1hEkpF28c982","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — this reframes a few things. Updated plan:\n\n**Audience reframe:** this is for a placement-application reader with ~2 minutes, not a general \"wow\" visitor. So the structure needs to deliver the essential facts fast and let the 3D/scroll work function as *optional depth* below the fold, not a gate in front of the information.\n\n**Content accuracy fixes, by section:**\n- **Formula Student** — state she joined October 2025, chassis sub-team. The team's 12th-place finish (July 2025) is mentioned as team context, explicitly dated and attributed to the team, not framed as her result. Her bracket work: \"simulated 18% weight reduction (CAD/FEA), not yet manufactured — machining scheduled for November.\" No claim of a built or tested part.\n- **Phone charger** — group of four, her scope = gear train + housing. Include the real outcome (four minutes of cranking for ~1% charge) rather than hiding it — reads as honest and technically literate, appropriate for a second-year.\n- **Bike co-op** — drop \"hundreds of bikes\" entirely; no invented number. Frame as \"mechanic since 2023\" with the nature of the work, not a count.\n- **No testimonials, no invented quotes or metrics anywhere.** Only figures that trace to the CV/blog/your corrections above.\n\n**Structural idea worth adding:** your job-card format (what the customer reported → what you found → parts → what you did → test ride) is a clean, honest template. If you can pull a couple of real entries from the co-op's cards or your workshop logbook, that becomes a strong, true \"how I work\" section — concrete process over claimed achievement. I won't invent entries; this only happens if you supply real ones.\n\n**Revised top-of-page priority:** name, program/year, placement goal, and a tight skills/project summary visible immediately with no animation gat